	// default track replaces the old one. Only a `ready` asset accepts a track (`409
	// asset_not_ready` otherwise, `409 conflict` while it is being deleted, `404` once deleted).
	// The track is stored under the asset's prefix, registered with the purge and added to the
	// asset's signed manifest, which is signed again. It is not encrypted: it is served only
	// through a playback session. Requires the `assets:write` scope. An asset of another tenant
	// is `not_found`.
	//
