	// CreateWebhookEndpointWithBodyWithResponse Register a webhook endpoint
	//
	// Registers an https URL that receives Cipherframe's events (ADR 0045). The response carries
	// the signing secret **once**, as `whsec_<base64>`, the form Standard Webhooks libraries take;
	// Cipherframe stores it wrapped by the key provider and cannot show it again (rotate it to
	// get a new one). `events` filters the kinds the endpoint receives; leave it out or empty for
	// every kind. A tenant may have 10 endpoints (`conflict` beyond that). The URL must be https,
	// without credentials, and must not name a private, loopback or link-local address: the check
	// runs here and again, on the resolved address, at every delivery. Audited. Requires the
	// `webhooks:manage` scope. The response is `no-store`.
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /v1/webhook-endpoints (the `CreateWebhookEndpoint` operationId).
