// PutBrandLogoWithBodyWithResponse Upload the tenant's brand logo
//
// Stores a new version of the tenant's brand logo and makes it current (M7-4, ADR 0049). The
// body is `multipart/form-data` with the member `file` and the optional `corner`, `opacity`
// and `enabled`. The file name the client sends is ignored and never stored or logged.
//
// The file must be a still PNG of at most 256 KB, between 16 and 1024 pixels on each side. It
// is checked before anything else touches it: the size, the PNG signature, the header's
// dimensions (so a tiny file that claims a huge image is refused before it is decoded), then a
// full decode by the server. An animated PNG is refused (`400`), as is an image that is fully
// transparent. The server then writes the picture again with its own PNG encoder and stores
// only that, so text, metadata and every other ancillary chunk of the upload are gone. A file
// that is not a PNG, is damaged or breaks a limit is `400 invalid_request` with a field error
// on `file` that never quotes it; one over 256 KB (before or after the rewrite) is `413`.
//
// `corner` is `top_left`, `top_right`, `bottom_left` or `bottom_right` (default
// `bottom_right`), `opacity` is a whole number of percent from 10 to 100 (default 100) and
// `enabled` is `true` or `false` (default `true`). The logo is drawn at 15 percent of the
// picture's width.
//
// **Not retroactive.** The logo is burned into the video when an asset is transcoded. A new
// logo, a changed placement and a removal apply only to assets whose processing starts
// afterwards. An asset that is being processed keeps the logo it started with, also across
// retries, and assets that are already ready keep theirs: there is no re-transcode. Old
// versions are removed once no asset in processing needs them. Requires the `admin` scope.
//
